commit 2cacb74c2811ab6f5e191b89816aea443dd6920d
Author: Wallace Chan <naahtec@hotmail.com>
Date:   Sat Jun 13 22:02:55 2026 -0400

    fix(#12142): preserve uncommitted WIP across context-pressure reboots
    
    Add _preserve_wip() to cycle_pre.main(), run BEFORE _enforce_branch and
    _do_pull. When the tree is dirty AND working-state names an in-progress
    task #N, commit code WIP to that task feature branch via git_ops
    commit-code (state/ephemeral files stay on the normal state->main route).
    Fail-open no-op on a clean tree (the normal post-commit case), so it only
    fires after a genuine mid-cycle reboot.
    
    Also align _get_branch_name fallback default to squidsquad/task/{number}
    (the #6526 git_ops canonical) so an independently-computed branch matches
    the one task-begin actually created.
    
    Tests: 8 TestPreserveWip cases (dirty/clean/not-in-progress/no-task/
    unparseable/state-only/fail-open/ordering) + QA-input branch-hint tests
    retargeted to the canonical pattern. 134 passed.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

